<%# The player a media post's template puts at the top: the post's own
    ```card type: player (HasMarkdownExtensions#template_player_card_html).
    Only rendered when Post#show_template_player? — no card in the body, and
    content.yml's players setting on.

    The duration isn't shown here: it's the card's `show_duration: true`,
    off by default, so the automatic player and a card written into the body
    look the same.

    The spacing is inline so it holds on every theme without an update:
    the card itself only has space above it, since in a post's body the
    paragraphs around it bring their own. %>
<div class="post-player" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-6, 1.5rem);">
  <%= post.template_player_card_html %>
</div>
